{"vid":"-XcALxwXJVY","source":"-XcALxwXJVY.en-GB.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":7.7,"txt":"Hello and welcome to 6 Minute English from BBC Learning English. I'm Neil."},{"t":12.1,"txt":"And I'm Pippa."},{"t":13.4,"txt":"Apps like Duolingo, Babbel and Busuu all aim to help you learn a language,"},{"t":18.4,"txt":"but do they really help?"},{"t":20,"txt":"We'll be trying to answer that question"},{"t":22,"txt":"in today's episode of 6 Minute English,"},{"t":24.2,"txt":"and as usual we'll be learning some useful new vocabulary too."},{"t":27.9,"txt":"Yes, and don't forget to head to our website for a transcript of this episode"},{"t":31.6,"txt":"and a free worksheet to test what you've learnt."},{"t":34.2,"txt":"It's all at bbclearningenglish.com."},{"t":37.2,"txt":"OK. Neil, let's start with a quiz question."},{"t":40.2,"txt":"Which of these is not a language you can learn using Duolingo?"},{"t":44.5,"txt":"Is it: a) Latin, b) Klingon, or c) Elvish?"},{"t":49.3,"txt":"I'm going to say c) Elvish."},{"t":52.7,"txt":"Well, we'll find out at the end of the programme."},{"t":55.5,"txt":"Now, people might be familiar with the app Duolingo."},{"t":58.8,"txt":"And then there are other apps which say they can help"},{"t":61.1,"txt":"you learn a language quickly – Bussuu and Babbel, for example."},{"t":65,"txt":"And listeners might be familiar with how they tend to work."},{"t":68.2,"txt":"You get short lessons which test you on a repeated set of words."},{"t":72.1,"txt":"Right. And many of these apps say they focus on teaching language"},{"t":75.8,"txt":"for situations and implicit learning,"},{"t":78.7,"txt":"rather than directly teaching language rules such as grammar."},{"t":82.1,"txt":"If something is implicit, it's suggested but not communicated directly."},{"t":86.5,"txt":"Yes. So, if you think about how children learn to speak their first language,"},{"t":90.8,"txt":"it's mostly implicit – they don't have lessons."},{"t":93.8,"txt":"But can this work for adults?"},{"t":96.1,"txt":"BBC Radio 4 programme Sliced Bread has been investigating the evidence"},{"t":100.3,"txt":"behind language learning apps."},{"t":102.2,"txt":"Presenter Greg Foot spoke to language learning expert"},{"t":104.9,"txt":"Professor Elizabeth Wonnacott, or Liz, about implicit learning."},{"t":109.3,"txt":"There is a very big difference between being a child"},{"t":112.7,"txt":"who gets constantly exposed to this world of language,"},{"t":116.2,"txt":"compared with trying to learn a language a few hours a week."},{"t":119.6,"txt":"There is quite a bit of evidence that some explicit teaching of,"},{"t":123.8,"txt":"for example, grammar and vocabulary is helpful."},{"t":126.4,"txt":"Got you. So, it would be helpful to try to mimic what children do,"},{"t":130.2,"txt":"which is full immersion,"},{"t":132,"txt":"but realistically you're not going to get to those levels."},{"t":135.8,"txt":"Liz says that while children learn their first language implicitly"},{"t":139.5,"txt":"by being constantly surrounded by the language,"},{"t":142.4,"txt":"adults are often learning for only a few hours a week."},{"t":145.7,"txt":"Yes. So, for adults trying to learn a new language,"},{"t":148.6,"txt":"research has shown that some explicit teaching is helpful."},{"t":152.1,"txt":"Explicit is the opposite of implicit."},{"t":154.3,"txt":"So, for example, explicit grammar teaching would be somebody explaining"},{"t":158.2,"txt":"a grammar rule to you."},{"t":159.9,"txt":"Right. So, adults can't realistically achieve full immersion"},{"t":163.6,"txt":"in a language like children do."},{"t":165.5,"txt":"Immersion means being completely surrounded by something."},{"t":168.6,"txt":"OK. So, a mixture of the implicit teaching of the apps and"},{"t":172.5,"txt":"some explicit teaching – for example, learning grammar rules – is useful."},{"t":176.5,"txt":"But Neil, there's limited research about"},{"t":178.8,"txt":"just how effective these apps can be at teaching you a language."},{"t":182.2,"txt":"Indeed, Liz Wonnacott has seen one study she thinks could be interesting though,"},{"t":187.1,"txt":"which compares two groups of Spanish speakers learning English –"},{"t":190.8,"txt":"one using an app and one attending classes – for a similar amount of time."},{"t":195.6,"txt":"She explains more to BBC Radio 4 programme Sliced Bread."},{"t":199.7,"txt":"The key finding was that in some of the tests, written grammar tests,"},{"t":203.3,"txt":"the Duolingo learners actually improved a bit more,"},{"t":206.4,"txt":"while actually in a test where they were looking"},{"t":208.2,"txt":"at listening the classroom learners appeared to improve more."},{"t":212.1,"txt":"So, it's really promising,"},{"t":214.3,"txt":"but of course it's one particular language, in one particular app,"},{"t":217.7,"txt":"against one particular school."},{"t":219.9,"txt":"Liz says the key finding"},{"t":221.6,"txt":"from the research is that the app users improved more on written tests,"},{"t":225.7,"txt":"but the classroom learners improved more on listening tests."},{"t":229.4,"txt":"A key finding is the most important conclusion of a piece of research."},{"t":233.4,"txt":"Liz says the study is promising, which means it shows signs of being positive."},{"t":238,"txt":"Yes. However, Liz points out the limits of the study."},{"t":241.2,"txt":"It's only looking at one particular language, one particular app"},{"t":245,"txt":"and one particular language school."},{"t":247.3,"txt":"The repetition of 'one particular' here means specific or individual,"},{"t":251.5,"txt":"and Liz would like to see research on more apps,"},{"t":253.9,"txt":"more types of teaching and also more different languages."},{"t":257.4,"txt":"Apps can help us learn some parts of a language, but"},{"t":260.4,"txt":"in this study they weren't as successful at improving listening skills,"},{"t":264.6,"txt":"and so Liz concludes that combining learning in apps with some other ways"},{"t":269.3,"txt":"of studying is the best way to try to improve your language skills."},{"t":273.2,"txt":"Probably moving forwards,"},{"t":275,"txt":"some combination of human teaching and these platforms to give us"},{"t":278.8,"txt":"that repetition is probably going to be the right direction."},{"t":282.2,"txt":"As teachers, we'd also suggest doing things that help you improve"},{"t":285.8,"txt":"different skills – speaking, listening, reading and writing."},{"t":289.1,"txt":"So, listening to podcasts or trying to practise speaking with"},{"t":292.7,"txt":"a language exchange partner could be things to combine with learning in apps."},{"t":297.1,"txt":"Find what works for you."},{"t":298.8,"txt":"I think it's time to find out the answer to the quiz question, Neil."},{"t":302.7,"txt":"I asked you which language you can't learn on Duolingo..."},{"t":307.1,"txt":"and you were right. It's c) Elvish,"},{"t":309.8,"txt":"but you can learn Latin and Klingon,"},{"t":311.8,"txt":"the fictional language from the TV series Star Trek, on Duolingo."},{"t":315.4,"txt":"And if you did want to improve your Elvish,"},{"t":317.8,"txt":"we did find an app specifically for that."},{"t":320.4,"txt":"Right. Let's recap the vocabulary we learned in this episode."},{"t":324,"txt":"'Implicit' means suggested, but not communicated directly."},{"t":327.8,"txt":"'Explicit' is the opposite of 'implicit'."},{"t":330.4,"txt":"It means something is communicated directly."},{"t":333.2,"txt":"'Immersion' is the state of being fully surrounded by something."},{"t":336.9,"txt":"The key finding of a research study is the most important conclusion"},{"t":341,"txt":"of the research."},{"t":342,"txt":"And the phrase 'one particular' means specific or individual."},{"t":346.2,"txt":"Once again, our six minutes are up."},{"t":348.4,"txt":"Test what you've learned with the worksheet on our website."},{"t":351.1,"txt":"And if you're interested to hear the full episode of Sliced Bread"},{"t":354.5,"txt":"about language-learning apps and the science behind them,"},{"t":357.5,"txt":"there's a link in the notes below this episode."},{"t":360.1,"txt":"Try listening on 0.5 speed"},{"t":362.7,"txt":"or in short sections if you find it too difficult to keep up."},{"t":366.2,"txt":"Bye for now!"},{"t":366.8,"txt":"Goodbye!"}],"words":[{"t":7.68,"w":"Hello"},{"t":7.68,"w":"and"},{"t":7.68,"w":"welcome"},{"t":7.68,"w":"to"},{"t":7.68,"w":"6"},{"t":7.68,"w":"Minute"},{"t":7.68,"w":"English"},{"t":7.68,"w":"from"},{"t":7.68,"w":"BBC"},{"t":7.68,"w":"Learning"},{"t":7.68,"w":"English."},{"t":7.68,"w":"I'm"},{"t":7.68,"w":"Neil."},{"t":12.08,"w":"And"},{"t":12.08,"w":"I'm"},{"t":12.08,"w":"Pippa."},{"t":13.44,"w":"Apps"},{"t":13.44,"w":"like"},{"t":13.44,"w":"Duolingo,"},{"t":13.44,"w":"Babbel"},{"t":13.44,"w":"and"},{"t":13.44,"w":"Busuu"},{"t":13.44,"w":"all"},{"t":13.44,"w":"aim"},{"t":13.44,"w":"to"},{"t":13.44,"w":"help"},{"t":13.44,"w":"you"},{"t":13.44,"w":"learn"},{"t":13.44,"w":"a"},{"t":13.44,"w":"language,"},{"t":18.4,"w":"but"},{"t":18.4,"w":"do"},{"t":18.4,"w":"they"},{"t":18.4,"w":"really"},{"t":18.4,"w":"help?"},{"t":20.04,"w":"We'll"},{"t":20.04,"w":"be"},{"t":20.04,"w":"trying"},{"t":20.04,"w":"to"},{"t":20.04,"w":"answer"},{"t":20.04,"w":"that"},{"t":20.04,"w":"question"},{"t":21.96,"w":"in"},{"t":21.96,"w":"today's"},{"t":21.96,"w":"episode"},{"t":21.96,"w":"of"},{"t":21.96,"w":"6"},{"t":21.96,"w":"Minute"},{"t":21.96,"w":"English,"},{"t":24.2,"w":"and"},{"t":24.2,"w":"as"},{"t":24.2,"w":"usual"},{"t":24.2,"w":"we'll"},{"t":24.2,"w":"be"},{"t":24.2,"w":"learning"},{"t":24.2,"w":"some"},{"t":24.2,"w":"useful"},{"t":24.2,"w":"new"},{"t":24.2,"w":"vocabulary"},{"t":24.2,"w":"too."},{"t":27.88,"w":"Yes,"},{"t":27.88,"w":"and"},{"t":27.88,"w":"don't"},{"t":27.88,"w":"forget"},{"t":27.88,"w":"to"},{"t":27.88,"w":"head"},{"t":27.88,"w":"to"},{"t":27.88,"w":"our"},{"t":27.88,"w":"website"},{"t":27.88,"w":"for"},{"t":27.88,"w":"a"},{"t":27.88,"w":"transcript"},{"t":27.88,"w":"of"},{"t":27.88,"w":"this"},{"t":27